# in a string every unescaped brace opens a placeholder {name}; a literal brace is \{ or \} (D-102)
** spec: lexical/lexical.md#string
driver a66_bad_placeholder is
  process main is
    print "pair {1, 2}";         ** lexical error: not a placeholder, write \{1, 2\}
  return;
end a66_bad_placeholder;
